concepts.content:
A recurrent layer is defined by the following equations: 
$$\begin{aligned}
    \mathbf{h}_t &= f(\mathbf{h}_{t-1}, \mathbf{x}_{\texttt{in}}[t]) &\triangleleft \quad\quad \text{update state based on input and previous state}\\
    \mathbf{x}_{\texttt{out}}[t]&= g(\mathbf{h}_t) &\triangleleft \quad\quad \text{produce output based on state}
\end{aligned}$$

This is a layer that includes a state variable, $\mathbf{h}$. The operation of the layer depends on its state. The layer also updates its state every time it is called; therefore, the state acts as a kind of memory.

